 "summary": "The new material (spin tensor operator, vector/tensor polarizations, spin-one Cartesian matrices, positivity bounds) has no counterpart in Mathlib, Physlib, PhyslibAlpha, QuantumInfo, TauCeti or EpsilonEridani, and it reuses the located upstream API where it exists: `Matrix.crossProductMatrix`/`crossProductMatrix_transpose`, `PauliMatrix.pauliMatrix_anticommutator`, `su2GenEntry`/`su2FundamentalStatement`, and TauCeti's `PosSemidef.normSq_le`. The `PosSemidef.lean` change generalizes rather than duplicates: the existing real `two_mul_abs_apply_le` is now derived from the new `RCLike` lemma in one line, and all three retained lemmas have consumers.",
